      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>And we beodað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.8"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.9"/> men ealles to swiðe of earde ne sylle ne on hæðendome<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.10"/> huru ne gebringe; ac beorge man georne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man þa saule<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.star"/> ne forfare, þe Crist mid his agenum life gebohte.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>We beodað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene men ealles to swiðe of eardan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.1"/> ne sylle ne on hæðendóme huru ne bringe; ac beorgan man georne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man ða sawla ne forfáre, ðe Crist mid his agenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>And we forbeodað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.2-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene menn ealles to swyþe of earde ne sylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-3"/> ne on hæðenedome<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man þa sawla ne forfare, þe Crist mid his agenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>[3] And witena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> gerædnes is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene men ealles to swiðe of earde ne sille ne on hæðendo<hi rend="italic">m</hi> huru ne gebrýnge; ac beorge man georne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man þa sawla ne forfare, þe Crist mid his agenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>Precipimus, ne Christiani<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.2"/> passim in exilium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-2"/> uenundentur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.4"/> (uendantur) uel in gentilitatem, ne forte pereant animę, quas propria uita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.5"/> sua mercatus est dominus noster Iesus Christus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>Et prohibemus, ne Christiani gentibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-4"/> extra hanc terram uenundentur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.4-3"/> nec in paganismo, ne anima Christiana, quam ipse Christus suo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.5-2"/> sanguine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.star-2"/> redemit, pereat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_3.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>[3] Interdicimus etiam, ne Christiani foras a patria uenundentur, presertim in paganism[um] non tradantur; sed diligenter parcatur animabus, quas Christus propria uita comparauit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="176" ed="#robertson"/>We beodað<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_3.robnote.fn.4"/> þæt man Cristene men ealles to swiðe of eardan ne sylle ne on hæðendóme huru ne bringe, ac beorgan man georne<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_3.robnote.fn.5"/>, þæt man ða sawla ne forfáre ðe Crist mid his agenum life gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="254" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we forbeodað þæt man Cristene men ealles to swiðe of earde ne sylle ne on hæðendome huru ne gebringe; ac beorge man georne þæt man þa saule ne forfare, þe Crist mid his agenum life gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_3.lnote.de.1"/> wir gebieten (verbieten <hi rend="italic">A</hi>; Beschluss der Witan ist <hi rend="italic">D</hi>), dass man christliche Menschen nicht allzu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_3.lnote.de.2"/> rasch ausser Landes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_3.lnote.de.3"/> verkaufe, wenigstens nicht ins Heidentum bringe; sondern ernstlich hüte man sich, dass man jene Seelen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_3.lnote.de.4"/> (-le <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) nicht verderbe, die Christus mit seinem eigenen Leben erkauft hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we command (forbid, A; it is the decision of the witan, D) that Christian people are not to be sold out of the country all too readily, at least not brought into heathendom; but let people take great care not to destroy those souls (that soul, G) which Christ bought with his own life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="177" ed="#robertson"/>We forbid the all too prevalent practice<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_3.robnote.n.2"/> of selling Christian people out of the country<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_3.robnote.n.3"/>, and especially of conveying them into heathen lands, but care shall be zealously taken that the souls which Christ bought with his own life be not destroyed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="255" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we forbid the all-too-common practice of selling Christians out of this land, and especially bringing them into heathen lands; but we must zealously ensure that the souls not be destroyed which Christ purchased with his own life.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="311"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_9">VI Atr 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_41">Leis Wl 41</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_41-1">Leis Wl 41.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_9">VI Atr 9</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 3: Cn 1018 6  VI Atr 9</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-014">Cn 1018 6</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 3: Cn 1018 6  VI Atr 9</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="68"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-014">Cn 1018 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_41">Leis Wl 41–41.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A skips a line (‘huru … georne’), as did the sources of Quadr. and the Instituta. The other MSS' ‘sawla’ (plural) is more original than G's ‘saule’. Liebermann compares VI Atr 9.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 311, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">forbeodað: beodað AG</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">huru . . . georne: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">paganis manu <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">paganis manu Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliqui <hi rend="italic">fügt zu K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliqui added by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lia <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lia Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uenu. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> uend. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uenu. K; uend. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uoluntate <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> ui. s. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uoluntate instead of ui. s. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forbe. [<hi rend="italic">vgl. A</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forbe. [cf. A] Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-en <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-en Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hæþened., <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> huru — georne [<hi rend="italic">wie A</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hæþened., without huru — georne [as A] Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sawla <hi rend="italic">übriger Hss. originaler; vgl. jedoch Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sawla of the other MSS more original; but cf. Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ht <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ht Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus VI Atr.</hi> 9?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from VI Atr. 9?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Inst., Consil.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Inst., Consil.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> syle</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from syle</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Zeile überspr.</hi> (<hi rend="italic">weil sie</hi> -orne, <hi rend="italic">wie vorige</hi> -ome, <hi rend="italic">endete</hi>) <hi rend="italic">auch in Vorlagen des Quadr. u. der Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">line skipped (because it ended in -orne, as the preceding one did in -ome), also in the exemplars of Quadr. and Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.3-4" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. h. t. gentilibus <hi rend="italic">LbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. h. t. gentilibus LbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uendantur <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uendantur Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sa. suo <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sa. suo Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. I</hi> 18, 3 <hi rend="italic">B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. I 18, 3 B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">4 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">4 lacking in Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Leis Wl 41 übersetzen das in AQInst Fehlende <hi rend="italic">ac beorge man georne</hi>; <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Einl. 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Leis Wl 41 translate the words <hi rend="italic">ac beorge man georne</hi>, which are missing in AQInst; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Introduction 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese Einschränkung ist geringer als die in <hi rend="italic">unforworhte</hi> VI Atr und bleibt fort in Wl; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> unfrei 12g</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This restriction is slighter than that in <hi rend="italic">unforworhte</hi> in VI Atr, and is omitted in Wl; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> unfrei 12g</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über die Endung in B's <hi rend="italic">eardan s. Wb</hi> S. 48 Sp. 2; die Form steht bei Layamon; Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the ending in B’s <hi rend="italic">eardan see Wb</hi> p. 48 col. 2; the form occurs in Layamon; Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cnut meint Plural laut vorherigen <hi rend="italic">men</hi>, trotz Hss.-Klasse gi</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut means the plural, as the preceding <hi rend="italic">men</hi> shows, despite the MS class gi</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_3.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 9; VII, 5.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_3.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann translates <hi rend="italic">ealles to swiðe</hi> as ‘allzu rasch,’ but is it not rather used elliptically, meaning ‘as is done far too much’? It can hardly have been intended at this time to give legal sanction to the practice at all.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_3.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With regard to the form <hi rend="italic">eardan</hi>, see I Atr. 2 and note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_3.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope></bibl><label>beodað</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">forbeodað</hi> A, Ld; <hi rend="italic">And witena</hi> &amp;c. D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_3.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope></bibl><label>georne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">huru—georne</hi> om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
